-republican-restraint-is/", "author_flair_class": "", "is_removed": false, "media": {"resized_resolutions": [], "blurhash": "", "full_resolution": []}, "title": "Sh*t or Get off the Pot.  GOP needs to decide if its a grand old party or gaytarded ocean of poops", "last_comment_created": 1794866122375, "content": "", "score_down": 0, "author_flair_text": "", "pro_tier": 0, "is_stickied": false, "is_nsfw": false, "is_deleted": false, "is_image": false, "comments": 7, "score_up": 64, "is_edited": false, "is_moderator": false, "awards": 0, "vote_state": 2, "link_metadata": {"description": "The next Congress has not convened, but its threatened investigations already bear the character of political theater.", "large_image": "1f73PE33KqIosWMz.png", "title": "The Era of Republican Restraint Is Over * The Gateway Pundit * by Publicola"}, "post_flair_text": "", "archive_id": ""}, {"is_locked": false, "tweet_id": "", "sticky_comment": 0, "is_video_mp4": false, "type": "text", "uuid": "1AToiJlNF3", "is_twitter": false, "is_admin": false, "score": 32, "suggested_sort": 0, "post_flair_class": "", "id": 8942729, "raw_content": "Written by Ali Velshi ---Staff leaks expose a Washington rut of canceled meetings, skipped obligations, and apparent indifference to the Pennsylvanians who sent him to the Senate.\nA bombshell investigation by The Wall Street Journal paints a staggering picture of Senator John Fetterman\u2019s approach to the job, based on internal text messages and interviews with more than a dozen former aides and lawmakers. The pattern is hard to miss.\nWhen officials from the Children\u2019s Hospital of Philadelphia asked to meet about concerns over Medicaid cuts, Fetterman dismissed them to an aide, saying he thought they just wanted \u201cfree trips to DC.\u201d\nThen came three paralyzed Pennsylvania veterans who traveled to the Capitol for a long-awaited meeting about legislation affecting their care.\nFetterman canceled, with staff telling the veterans he wasn\u2019t feeling well after possibly eating something bad.\nLess than an hour later, he was back in his office and headed for a Fox News interview about Israel and the war in Iran.\nThe Journal also reports that Fetterman skipped a funeral for three Pennsylvania police officers killed in the line of duty after learning the service would last three hours.\nPennsylvania constituents seeking help with flood relief were reportedly ignored as Fetterman walked past them in the Capitol.\nAnd Senate hearings became something of a drive-by: aides described a practice of briefly sticking his head into committee rooms so he could be marked present before leaving.\nThis isn\u2019t about whether Fetterman is progressive enough, conservative enough, or sufficiently loyal to either political party. It\u2019s about whether he is doing the job.A United States senator is elected to represent actual human beings\u2014not just cable-news audiences, political allies, or causes he happens to care about.\nPennsylvanians did not elect a ghost senator to collect a paycheck while treating constituent meetings, Senate hearings, fallen police officers, hospitalized children and disabled veterans as inconveniences. They elected a United States senator.\nAnd according to the evidence laid out by The Wall Street Journal, John Fetterman increasingly seems to regard that job as an inconvenience of its own.\n\u2014\u2014\nSPREAD THE WORD. Like, comment, follow, and share. Thank you for your support.....", "author": "Toobigtorig1234", "created": 1794870532981, "profile_picture": "", "community": "TheDonald", "ad_tier": 2, "last_comment_author": "dagthegnome", "is_video": false, "video_link": "", "is_new_user": false, "domain": "", "is_crosspost": false, "preview": "", "removal_source": "", "link": "", "author_flair_class": "", "is_removed": false, "media": {"resized_resolutions": [], "blurhash": "", "full_resolution": []}, "title": "Hello PA...The set up to dismiss Fetterman and prop up another DSA muslim has begun..", "last_comment_created": 1794871696948, "content": "<p>Written by Ali Velshi ---Staff leaks expose a Washington rut of canceled meetings, skipped obligations, and apparent indifference to the Pennsylvanians who sent him to the Senate.\nA bombshell investigation by The Wall Street Journal paints a staggering picture of Senator John Fetterman\u2019s approach to the job, based on internal text messages and interviews with more than a dozen former aides and lawmakers. The pattern is hard to miss.\nWhen officials from the Children\u2019s Hospital of Philadelphia asked to meet about concerns over Medicaid cuts, Fetterman dismissed them to an aide, saying he thought they just wanted \u201cfree trips to DC.\u201d\nThen came three paralyzed Pennsylvania veterans who traveled to the Capitol for a long-awaited meeting about legislation affecting their care.\nFetterman canceled, with staff telling the veterans he wasn\u2019t feeling well after possibly eating something bad.\nLess than an hour later, he was back in his office and headed for a Fox News interview about Israel and the war in Iran.\nThe Journal also reports that Fetterman skipped a funeral for three Pennsylvania police officers killed in the line of duty after learning the service would last three hours.\nPennsylvania constituents seeking help with flood relief were reportedly ignored as Fetterman walked past them in the Capitol.\nAnd Senate hearings became something of a drive-by: aides described a practice of briefly sticking his head into committee rooms so he could be marked present before leaving.\nThis isn\u2019t about whether Fetterman is progressive enough, conservative enough, or sufficiently loyal to either political party. It\u2019s about whether he is doing the job.A United States senator is elected to represent actual human beings\u2014not just cable-news audiences, political allies, or causes he happens to care about.\nPennsylvanians did not elect a ghost senator to collect a paycheck while treating constituent meetings, Senate hearings, fallen police officers, hospitalized children and disabled veterans as inconveniences. They elected a United States senator.\nAnd according to the evidence laid out by The Wall Street Journal, John Fetterman increasingly seems to regard that job as an inconvenience of its own.\n\u2014\u2014\nSPREAD THE WORD. Like, comment, follow, and share. Thank you for your support.....</p>\n", "score_down": 0, "author_flair_text": "", "pro_tier": 0, "is_stickied": false, "is_nsfw": false, "is_deleted": false, "is_image": false, "comments": 2, "score_up": 32, "is_edited": false, "is_moderator": false, "awards": 0, "vote_state": 2, "link_metadata": {"status": 200}, "post_flair_text": "", "archive_id": ""}, {"is_locked": false, "tweet_id": "2122320094827106568", "sticky_comment": 0, "is_video_mp4": false, "type": "link", "uuid": "1AToiJk0KT", "is_twitter": true, "is_admin": false, "score": 119, "suggested_sort": 0, "post_flair_class": "", "id": 8942275, "raw_content": "", "author": "Capoditutticapi1", "created": 1794844812946, "profile_picture": "", "community": "TheDonald", "ad_tier": 2, "last_comment_author": "goatnuts", "is_video": false, "video_link": "", "is_new_user": false, "domain": "twitter.com", "is_crosspost": false, "preview": "https://media.scored.co/preview/1AToiJk0KT.png", "removal_source": "", "link": "https://twitter.com/SoveyX/status/2122320094827106568?a=fn4dfw4B3YhgTXlqn5Q&s=20", "author_flair_class": "", "is_removed": false, "media": {"resized_resolutions": [], "blurhash": "", "full_resolution": []}, "title": "Jensen is back! ", "last_comment_created": 1794865434628, "content": "", "score_down": 0, "author_flair_text": "", "pro_tier": 0, "is_stickied": false, "is_nsfw": false, "is_deleted": false, "is_image": false, "comments": 8, "score_up": 119, "is_edited": false, "is_moderator": false, "awards": 0, "vote_state": 2, "link_metadata": {"twitter": {"quotedTweet": false, "images": false, "linkEmbed": false, "repl